# hexagonrpcd — the FastRPC file server for Qualcomm Hexagon DSPs, built FROM SOURCE via a
# retroforge-owned PKGBUILD (packages/hexagonrpcd/PKGBUILD). The ADSP's sensors PD on the Air X
# reads its registry and configs through it. Not in the holo snapshot.
#
# After adding or bumping this: `make relock` (the package must land in rootfs/manifest.lock; it is
# listed in PKGS in rootfs/customize-base.sh).
#
# Patches:
#   0001  ours: the ADSP units no longer conflict with suspend.target, which stopped them for good.
#   0002  kettlelinux's (via Armada), backported: answer a request hexagonrpcd cannot serve
#         instead of exiting, which left the ADSP's caller waiting and the ADSP awake for good.
#   0003-0006  kettlelinux's (gennro): serve sns_reg_version, serve sensors/persist writable when
#         the tree has it, input buffers over 256 bytes, methods from 31 on. The Pocket FIT's
#         sensors PD rebuilds its registry at every start; refused, it took the ADSP down.
name: hexagonrpcd
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
patches: 0001-data-keep-the-ADSP-servers-running-across-suspend.patch 0002-hexagonrpcd-answer-a-request-it-cannot-serve-and-kee.patch 0003-hexagonrpcd-serve-the-sensors-registry-version-file.patch 0004-hexagonrpcd-a-writable-persist-sensors-directory.patch 0005-hexagonrpcd-fetch-large-input-buffers.patch 0006-hexagonrpcd-methods-from-31-on.patch
pkgrel_suffix: 1
